        "original_id": "e1548e4c-95ac-53d3-8341-0e989b1118d4",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Mikael Åkerfeldt, Lee Ranaldo, Thurston Moore, Steven Wilson\n- Bands/Projects: Opeth, Bloodbath, Steel, Storm Corrosion, Sonic Youth\n- Publications/Rankings: Rolling Stone, Spin\n- Songs/Albums: \"Youth Against Fascism\", Dirty\n\nFacts:\n- Mikael Åkerfeldt, born on 17 April 1974, is a Swedish musician.\n- Lee Ranaldo, born on February 3, 1956, is an American musician, singer-songwriter, guitarist, writer, visual artist, and record producer.\n- \"Youth Against Fascism\" was the second single from Sonic Youth's 1992 album Dirty.\n- In 2004, Rolling Stone ranked Lee Ranaldo at number 33 on its \"Greatest Guitarists of All Time\" list.\n- In May 2012, Spin ranked Thurston Moore and his Sonic Youth bandmate Lee Ranaldo together at number 1 in a staff-selected top 100 list.\n- Mikael Åkerfeldt is the lead vocalist, guitarist, and primary songwriter of Opeth.\n- Mikael Åkerfeldt is the former vocalist of Bloodbath.\n- Mikael Åkerfeldt was also guitarist for the one-off band Steel.\n- Mikael Åkerfeldt is part of Storm Corrosion with Steven Wilson.\n- Lee Ranaldo is best known as a co-founder of Sonic Youth.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
